      "id": 1,
      "text": "Archaeologists found prehistoric Native American artifacts in the area that would become Prattsville, showing human presence long before European settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/prattsville_arkansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Prattsville was named for pioneer John Pratt, who arrived around 1850, and the town grew around cotton ginning before officially incorporating in 1962.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/prattsville_arkansas",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A railroad built between 1899 and 1900 linked Sheridan to Pine Bluff, boosting log transport and bringing Prattsville into regional markets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/prattsville_arkansas",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A historical marker north of Prattsville in the pioneer Village of Belfast commemorates the town, though the access road is now gated.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prattsville%2C_Arkansas",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Prattsville faces frequent thunderstorms, high humidity that fuels insects, and a notable tornado risk as part of Arkansas’s Dixie Alley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/prattsville_arkansas",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The town sits on gently rolling terrain about 290 feet high, draining into the Saline River basin and occasionally flooding low areas.",
